    "# Gas processing value chain with NeqSim\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook builds a reproducible wellhead-to-sales-gas calculation with NeqSim 3.16.0 or\n",
    "newer. It connects thermodynamic phase behavior, offshore separation and compression, export\n",
    "pipeline hydraulics, onshore NGL extraction, ISO 6976 gas quality, and energy/emissions screening.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Learning objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "After completing the notebook, you can:\n",
    "\n",
    "- create and condition a multicomponent reservoir fluid with the Pengâ€“Robinson equation of state;\n",
    "- compose NeqSim streams and unit operations into converged process systems;\n",
    "- retrieve duties, powers, product rates, compositions, and phase envelopes with explicit units;\n",
    "- size screening-level coolers, heaters, scrubbers, and an export line;\n",
    "- check product specifications, conservation, and numerical trends; and\n",
    "- reuse a parameterized compression workflow for engineering sensitivity studies.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an educational screening model, not a substitute for project design assurance.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "1lhtWDzYrV92"
   },
   "source": [
    "## Basis and assumptions\n",
    "\n",
    "The assignment represents a 20 GSmÂ³/year wet reservoir-gas stream flowing from a subsea well to\n",
    "an offshore platform, then through a 700 km export line and an onshore liquids-recovery process.\n",
    "Temperatures, pressures, compositions, and standard-flow units are declared below. Cooling-water\n",
    "and heating-medium temperatures are screening assumptions; equipment margins, pressure losses,\n",
    "control ranges, material limits, and dynamic operability require separate study.\n"
   ]
  },
