   "source": [
    "## Q4 â€” Heat-transfer area screening\n",
    "\n",
    "Use an overall heat-transfer coefficient $U=1000$ W/(mÂ² K). Cooling water enters at 5 Â°C and\n",
    "leaves at 20 Â°C; heating medium enters at 120 Â°C and leaves at 60 Â°C. For counter-current flow,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Q=UA\\Delta T_{lm}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Delta T_{lm}=\\frac{\\Delta T_1-\\Delta T_2}{\\ln(\\Delta T_1/\\Delta T_2)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $Q$ is heat duty in W, $A$ is area in mÂ², and both terminal temperature differences are in\n",
    "K. The code checks that terminal differences are positive before applying the equation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "EX3qFrw-NVx0"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "overall_heat_transfer_coefficient = 1000.0  # W/(mÂ² K)\n",
    "cooling_water_inlet_temperature = 5.0  # Â°C\n",
    "cooling_water_outlet_temperature = 20.0  # Â°C\n",
    "heating_medium_inlet_temperature = 120.0  # Â°C\n",
    "heating_medium_outlet_temperature = 60.0  # Â°C\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def log_mean_temperature_difference(delta_t_1, delta_t_2):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return counter-current LMTD in K after checking physical terminal differences.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if delta_t_1 <= 0.0 or delta_t_2 <= 0.0:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Both terminal temperature differences must be positive.\")\n",
    "    if math.isclose(delta_t_1, delta_t_2, rel_tol=1.0e-12):\n",
    "        return 0.5 * (delta_t_1 + delta_t_2)\n",
    "    return (delta_t_1 - delta_t_2) / math.log(delta_t_1 / delta_t_2)\n"
   ]
  },
